NUM-19: book an outfall's net flow when it both receives and sends flow

The outfall branch of updateRoutingMassBalance() follows legacy
node_getSystemOutflow(): inflow when the outfall has no outflow, minus the
outflow when it has no inflow, and nothing when it has both. Two ordinary
cases give both: a FLOW (or DWF, RDII, ...) inflow at an outfall that feeds
the network, and every SKIP_STEADY_STATE step that follows a step on which
this pass set a feeding outfall's inflow to its outflow for reporting. Book
the net flow, inflow - outflow; remember which outfalls had their inflow
set for reporting, and on a skipped step book them with no inflow. Same
change as the 5.3.0 patch; the FV branch is not touched.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-19_swmm600.patch

